<h1>Plan: My Clay Hub D-4 — the weekly vault export (and scheduled functions in the guard)</h1>

<div class="meta">
  <strong>Goal:</strong> Every week, a complete copy of My Clay Hub's database lands in its own bucket in <code>tinker-hq-vault</code>, outside the <code>my-clay-hub</code> project. Christie gets an email if an export fails, and a separate email when no complete export has landed for 8 days, for any reason. The copy can be restored by following a written runbook. The function is deployed only through the functions guard, which now understands scheduled functions and checks Christie's reading of the Scheduler job.<br>
  <strong>Repo:</strong> <code>/Users/christiehubley/my-clay-hub</code>. Console work in <code>my-clay-hub</code> and <code>tinker-hq-vault</code> (Christie; no gcloud). Nothing in <code>tinker-hq-apps</code> or studio-hub changes.<br>
  <strong>Parent plans:</strong> <code>my-clay-hub-phase-d-project.html</code> D-4 (the outline this plan expands; see <a href="#trace">Traceability</a>), C2, C3; <code>firebase-functions-deploy-guard.html</code> (Phase D2) amendment <strong>M6</strong> and choice <strong>F13</strong>, which this plan amends for schedules only; <code>clayhub-members-foundation.html</code> (the Phase E gate).<br>
  <strong>Gate it lifts:</strong> Phase E loads no real member data until V-4 is complete: the newest <code>vault</code> attempt has <code>deploy_verified=yes</code>, <code>iam_attested=yes</code> and <code>scheduler_attested=yes</code>, and one complete export is in the vault bucket.<br>
  <strong>Not in this plan:</strong> any other trigger kind (events, callables, task queues, blocking); secrets or params; deleting functions; a retention lock on the vault bucket (V12); <code>tinker-hq-apps</code>' own functions guard (Phase E, M1); member data (the database is still empty).<br>
  <strong>Risk:</strong> MEDIUM. It changes the deploy guard, creates the project's first scheduled job, and adds the first grants <em>into</em> <code>tinker-hq-vault</code> from <code>my-clay-hub</code>. The database is empty and deny-all, so an export reads nothing sensitive yet.<br>
  <strong>History:</strong> Oct 1 written; review round 1 (Codex "not ready", 5 blocking; Claude "ready after fixes", 5 blocking) → this rewrite, with Christie's decisions O5/O6. See <a href="#reviews">Reviews</a>.<br>
  <strong>Status:</strong> <span class="status-tag not-ready">execution-ready: false</span> (all phases) — round 2 review next.
</div>

